  "problem": "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}x, & 0<x<4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf the probability density function of $Y=\\frac{1}{2}|X-1|$ is given by \n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}g(y), & 0<y<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ h(y), & \\frac{1}{2}\\le y<\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind the function $g(y).$",
